00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:42.410
episode

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:42.410
"The Angel's Secret"

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:49.000
Countess Polignac, I've been waiting for you.

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:51.350
Please come in.

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:52.820
Let's play some card games.

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:54.980
Lady Antoinette...

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:58.350
Actually, I came to say goodbye today.

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:05.900
<i>My... My Countess Polignac...!</i>

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:07.490
<i>Why?! Why is that?!</i>

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:11.350
It hasn't been that long since you
moved to the Palace, so why?

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:19.790
Your Majesty, your warm and generous
friendship has made us close,

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:26.780
but because I have no a rank or fortune,
I feel embarrassed to appear at court.

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:30.620
I can't even provide my daughter
with a proper dress to wear.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:34.460
Let alone the number of servants
and the size of our stable...

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:38.750
Just thinking about how embarrassed
my husband must feel, I...

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:41.990
I believe it's best we withdraw
ourselves from court...

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:43.830
Countess Polignac.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:46.340
Do not worry.

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:48.640
You mustn't withdraw from court.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:51.980
Why didn't you tell me this sooner?

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:54.510
Who do you regard me as?

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:56.150
I am the Queen of France.

00:04:57.050 --> 00:04:59.620
My dear friend, Countess Polignac.

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:03.200
I will instruct the Minister of Finance
to create a new budget for you.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.550
Your Majesty...!

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:07.720
On the palace grounds, I'll
have them build a stable...

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:11.360
...specifically for the Polignac family and increase
\hthe number of your horses and carriages five fold.

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:14.770
Your servants' salaries will
be paid by the country,

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:18.130
and I will assign your husband, Count Polignac,
to the position of Minister of Posts.

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:23.470
My goodness, what an angel
she turned out to be!

00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:27.010
She has such a sweet face, but in fact
she's as cunning as they come!

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:29.250
Her Majesty is too naïve!

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:31.920
Count Polignac as Minister of Posts?!

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:33.980
What past accomplishments does he even have?!

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:37.060
Not only that, his salary is 54,000 livres!

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:39.440
Good grief, how could this be?

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:50.950
Mother!

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.910
My dress...! Look at this wonderful dress!

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:56.800
I hardly recognize myself.

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:58.920
Charlotte.

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:04.880
The Polignac family has been in ruins,
burdened with endless debts,

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:06.170
but now, from this day forward...

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:10.090
<i>After all, the Queen is on my side now.</i>

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:25.500
<i>How... How gratifying!</i>

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:29.030
<i>I was able to make a dear friend happy!</i>

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:35.840
<i>She came to believe if she were happy,
the people would be happy, as well.</i>

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:41.010
<i>It was the first mistake Marie Antoinette would make.</i>

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:00.560
Father, I've just returned.

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:08.150
You fool!

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:17.490
Oscar, how dare you carelessly go out traveling,
while under disciplinary confinement!

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:19.430
Didn't you think about the trouble...

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:22.290
...this would cause Lady Antoinette,
if the court were to find out?!

00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:31.370
You engaged in a duel with a member
of a powerful ducal family.

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:36.240
Realizing that you could be
permanently exiled from court,

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:39.980
Lady Antoinette struck you with
a disciplinary confinement instead.

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:42.310
Don't you understand why she did that?

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:45.810
Forgive me, Father.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:47.620
However...

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:51.190
No, that's precisely why I left,
for Lady Antoinette's sake!

00:07:51.190 --> 00:07:55.460
To learn how the farmers who make up
the majority of France's population live!

00:07:55.460 --> 00:08:00.630
I wanted to know what they think and
how they view Lady Antoinette!

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:05.230
The lives of the farmers
I visited were dreadfully poor.

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:08.300
Can you imagine...

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:10.340
...why they are so poor, Father?

00:08:11.540 --> 00:08:15.100
Imagine a family dinner where
everyone must split one potato...

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:20.350
Something must be done soon!

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:22.690
Otherwise... Otherwise, something
terrible will happen someday!

00:08:24.890 --> 00:08:27.290
As an officer of the Royal Guards
serving the Queen,

00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:29.150
it's nothing you should be concerned with!

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:33.830
Understand?!

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:36.820
You are a noble and the Regiment
Commander of the Royal Guards!

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:42.500
If you have the time to think about such things,
use that time to better your sword skills!

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:49.370
<i>Oscar...</i>

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:54.190
To Hell with the nobility!

00:08:54.190 --> 00:08:55.010
To Hell with the Dukes!

00:08:57.320 --> 00:08:58.290
Oscar...

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:11.100
My, my!

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:13.040
If it isn't Countess Polignac!

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:15.070
Thank you for coming all this way!

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:17.980
I would have gladly visited, if you had sent for me!

00:09:17.980 --> 00:09:21.490
I need to have a new dress
made for a ball in a hurry.

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:21.980
Yes, certainly!

00:09:21.980 --> 00:09:25.440
We have specially made satins and
damask patterned fabrics in stock.

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:29.760
If you can't sew, you'll have to work in the kitchen.

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:31.990
Yes, that's fine.

00:09:31.990 --> 00:09:34.030
I'll do anything and work really hard.

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:36.220
So please allow me to work here!

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:37.900
Well...

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:39.100
Please!

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:42.600
There's a customer from Versailles, so hurry it up.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:43.830
Oh, I'll be right there.

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:45.600
Um...!

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:47.740
Fine then, you'll start tomorrow.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:51.670
Thank you very much!

00:09:57.820 --> 00:10:00.050
Thank you for your patronage.

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:01.660
We look forward to serving you again soon.

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:19.530
I'll finally be able to make things better for Mom.

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:22.850
I'll be able to buy her medicine and
take her to the doctor now, too.

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:35.910
Watch out!

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:44.430
All right then!

00:10:44.430 --> 00:10:46.360
I'd better go tell Mom the good news!

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:47.850
She'll be so happy!

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.970
Rosalie! Rosalie!

00:10:51.970 --> 00:10:52.670
Ma'am!

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:53.570
Rosalie!

00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:54.470
It's terrible!

00:10:54.470 --> 00:10:56.590
Your mother was run over by a carriage!

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:00.810
No, that can't be...!

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:32.140
Mom!

00:11:33.780 --> 00:11:36.580
Mom! What are you doing here, out of bed?!

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:38.650
Rosalie...

00:11:38.650 --> 00:11:40.210
I-I'm sorry...

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:40.210
Mom!

00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:49.530
What are you doing?!

00:11:49.530 --> 00:11:50.890
Hurry up and move the carriage!

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:52.350
Y-Yes...!

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:53.400
Wait!

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:54.900
Do you think you can just run away like this?!

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:56.990
You practically killed her outright!

00:11:57.870 --> 00:12:00.570
Why don't you come out of
the carriage and apologize?!

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:03.450
Do you think you can get away with
anything as long as you're a noble?!

00:12:03.940 --> 00:12:06.410
Don't accuse me of such things.

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:08.970
It's her own fault for running out
in front of the carriage suddenly.

00:12:12.420 --> 00:12:13.370
Stop!

00:12:13.820 --> 00:12:16.840
If you have a problem, come see me at Versailles.

00:12:18.220 --> 00:12:19.220
Come back here!

00:12:19.220 --> 00:12:20.190
Mom!

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:29.730
Rosalie, you're not my real daughter...

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:35.110
Rosalie, please forgive me...

00:12:35.110 --> 00:12:36.170
Mom...!

00:12:36.170 --> 00:12:40.670
Your real mother is... a n-noble...

00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:44.670
Mar...tine... Gabrielle...

00:12:46.580 --> 00:12:47.750
A noble...

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:50.540
Martine... Gabrielle...

00:12:51.190 --> 00:12:56.790
I'm really sorry... for all the
hardships I've caused you...

00:12:58.760 --> 00:12:59.750
Mom!

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:01.600
Mom!

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:03.300
Mom! No!

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:05.040
Don't leave me by myself!

00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:07.220
Don't leave me all alone!

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:10.400
Mom!

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:17.250
Hey, Guards! Wake up!

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:19.240
Her Majesty's carriage has returned!

00:13:25.090 --> 00:13:28.930
Good grief, another night at the ball, huh?

00:13:28.930 --> 00:13:30.700
Paris is that entertaining, eh?

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:36.400
My, Madame Jarjayes.

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:38.830
Welcome back, Your Majesty.

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:40.910
Oh...

00:13:40.910 --> 00:13:44.310
Madame Jarjayes, you look unwell.

00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:48.110
It isn't necessary for you to stay up
all night and wait for my return.

00:13:48.110 --> 00:13:50.850
Y-Yes, thank you.

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:53.650
Come, get some rest in your room.

00:13:53.650 --> 00:13:55.020
You seem really strained.

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:56.810
Yes, just for a little while then.

00:14:07.600 --> 00:14:10.330
<i>You... You killed my mother...!</i>

00:14:23.310 --> 00:14:24.340
Mom...

00:14:28.770 --> 00:14:32.040
<i>If you have a problem, come see me at Versailles!</i>

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:35.170
<i>Come see me at Versailles!</i>

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:40.950
<i>A blue floral patterned dress...</i>

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:43.140
<i>Blonde hair with curls...</i>

00:14:45.890 --> 00:14:48.260
How long do you intend on mourning here?

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:51.230
I know it's hard, but the dead won't come back.

00:14:52.330 --> 00:14:54.200
I'm Bernard Châtelet.

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:55.570
A journalist based in Paris.

00:14:55.570 --> 00:14:57.540
If you ever need anything,
you can come talk to me anytime.

00:14:58.300 --> 00:15:01.170
Thank you, but it's all right.

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:04.590
H-Hey! Mademoiselle!

00:15:08.480 --> 00:15:09.950
<i>Mom.</i>

00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:11.240
<i>I promise...</i>

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:13.850
<i>I promise to avenge you.</i>

00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:24.160
Um, is this the right way to Versailles?

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:24.930
Yeah.

00:15:24.930 --> 00:15:26.190
Thank you very much.

00:15:28.130 --> 00:15:29.670
Hey! Just so you know!

00:15:29.670 --> 00:15:32.870
It's going to be nightfall by the time you get there!

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:47.920
My, the moon was shining beautifully
just a moment ago, too.

00:15:48.650 --> 00:15:52.390
When I was young, I heard a fairytale that went like this.

00:15:52.860 --> 00:15:54.850
When the full moon hides behind the clouds,

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:57.650
it's because there's a girl crying somewhere...

00:15:58.960 --> 00:16:00.390
<i>Mom!</i>

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:03.290
What's the matter, Madame Polignac?

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:07.700
It's nothing, Your Majesty.

00:16:08.770 --> 00:16:10.840
Here, the night wind is bad for you.

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:12.320
Let's play some cards.

00:16:13.010 --> 00:16:14.010
All right.

00:16:14.010 --> 00:16:17.010
I learned how to play a new card game.

00:16:17.010 --> 00:16:18.380
My, how wonderful!

00:16:18.380 --> 00:16:19.540
Let's play it, then.

00:16:25.890 --> 00:16:26.910
Madame Jarjayes!

00:16:27.990 --> 00:16:29.560
Please wake up!

00:16:29.560 --> 00:16:30.880
Madame Jarjayes!

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:39.100
<i>It's nothing you should be concerned with!</i>

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:39.840
<i>Understand?!</i>

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:42.270
<i>You are a noble and the Regiment
Commander of the Royal Guards!</i>

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:45.270
<i>If you have the time to think about such things,
use that time to better your sword skills!</i>

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:07.330
Oscar!

00:17:07.330 --> 00:17:08.880
Madame has collapsed at the Palace!

00:17:09.900 --> 00:17:10.590
My mother has...?!

00:17:32.720 --> 00:17:35.560
Almost there... I'm almost at Versailles...

00:17:42.070 --> 00:17:42.970
I'm counting on you.

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:51.460
Lady Antoinette!

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:53.130
Oscar!

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:55.010
Please stop the carriage!

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:56.650
Oscar...

00:17:56.650 --> 00:17:59.970
Please forgive me for coming, even though
my disciplinary confinement isn't over yet.

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:02.420
Take good care of your mother.

00:18:02.420 --> 00:18:05.190
Let her rest and recuperate for a while.

00:18:05.190 --> 00:18:09.440
In her stead, please report to the
Palace starting tomorrow, Oscar.

00:18:11.100 --> 00:18:11.900
Then...?!

00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:14.470
The confinement period was a month.

00:18:14.470 --> 00:18:17.360
According to my calendar,
it's already long past, Oscar.

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:19.770
Lady Antoinette...

00:18:19.770 --> 00:18:22.470
Thank you... Thank you very much!

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:23.440
Your Majesty.

00:18:23.440 --> 00:18:26.910
We should leave soon or we'll be late for the ball.

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:27.370
All right.

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:29.350
Well then, see you tomorrow, Oscar.

00:18:29.350 --> 00:18:30.040
Yes!

00:18:41.130 --> 00:18:43.490
Are you all right, Mother?

00:18:44.090 --> 00:18:45.600
Why don't you lie down?

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:49.160
Thank you, Oscar.

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:51.300
I'm all right.

00:18:51.300 --> 00:18:53.500
I was only a little fatigued.

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:57.360
It's been a while, so relaxing
at home sounds rather nice.

00:19:06.380 --> 00:19:06.830
Here she comes!

00:19:12.060 --> 00:19:14.160
Here, Mother.

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:15.430
Please watch your step.

00:19:15.430 --> 00:19:16.830
Thank you, Oscar.

00:19:18.160 --> 00:19:19.290
It's definitely her!

00:19:19.900 --> 00:19:21.970
A blue floral pattered dress...!

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:23.260
Blonde hair with curls...!

00:19:24.400 --> 00:19:25.730
Mom's killer!

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:33.530
This is for killing my mother! Say your prayers!

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:37.380
What do you think you're doing?!

00:19:42.590 --> 00:19:43.520
You're...!

00:19:44.090 --> 00:19:45.060
You're...!

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:56.500
No...!

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:57.130
It's not her!

00:19:59.100 --> 00:20:00.430
It's not that woman!

00:20:18.320 --> 00:20:19.190
What?

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:21.700
You mistook this manor for
the Palace of Versailles?

00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:26.300
Well... I was told Versailles was this way!

00:20:26.300 --> 00:20:28.660
So when I saw this large palace, I thought...

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:30.830
What are you doing?!

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:32.060
Just come with me!

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:36.420
Wh-Where... Where are you taking me to?!

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:50.140
Come, have a look.

00:20:51.620 --> 00:20:55.430
Listen closely, Versailles is a city in itself.

00:20:55.430 --> 00:20:58.790
The royal palace is that giant
structure located further back.

00:21:09.770 --> 00:21:11.210
Now do you understand?

00:21:11.210 --> 00:21:15.180
No matter what you do, you won't be able
to sneak in, not even into the gardens.

00:21:15.180 --> 00:21:17.580
That woman is there...

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:20.250
You mentioned the woman
who killed your mother...

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:23.250
...wore a blue floral pattered dress.

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:25.960
However, every lady of the
court owns at least one...

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:28.580
...blue floral pattered dress
made of damask fabric.

00:21:31.730 --> 00:21:32.920
It makes me so angry...

00:21:33.630 --> 00:21:35.390
I didn't know a thing...

00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:38.700
My mother was killed in front of me...

00:21:38.700 --> 00:21:41.070
...but people like us can't do anything about it.

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:46.570
I'll teach you how to use a sword.

00:21:49.710 --> 00:21:53.650
Unfortunately, you won't be able to kill
even a puppy with your unsteady hands.

00:21:53.650 --> 00:21:58.540
If you truly wish to avenge your mother,
you'll need to learn how to use a sword.

00:21:59.420 --> 00:22:04.820
It'll be difficult to find the lady who killed
your mother, out of thousands of women,

00:22:04.820 --> 00:22:06.520
but there's no need to rush.

00:22:06.930 --> 00:22:08.970
As long as you have access to the Palace,

00:22:08.970 --> 00:22:11.890
I'm sure you'll come face
to face with her someday.

00:22:12.370 --> 00:22:13.740
In order to do that,

00:22:13.740 --> 00:22:17.700
you'll need to become a full-fledged lady
who can hold her own at court.

00:22:28.450 --> 00:22:32.830
To be continued

